# fixedbugs, defect 585, lane b19-pack, 2026-10-10.
#
# SYMPTOM: under a header of the program's own defining `_POSIX_C_SOURCE
# 200112L`, a name another header declares only where no POSIX level
# narrows it was told *declares no `wide_only`*, true and short of the
# cause: on this Mac `string.h`'s `strlcpy` was told so. These headers hide
# their name as Darwin does, on every platform.
#
# FIX: a refused round reads which strict switch each header leaves defined
# and asks the headers again with it undefined after the one that defines
# it (`cli/unswitch_ask.hero`); a name declared there is told with the
# switch and the header.

extern "fixedbugs-585-strict.h"
    function strict_on() -> i64

extern "fixedbugs-585-wide.h"
    function wide_only() -> i64  #~ ffi_unknown_name

function main()
    print(strict_on() + wide_only())
